        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree e06d68a7122da9364765c2c09bcebdb85303fbee\nparent 69142eacd1374925cc9e4ea736c21fcec16307d0\nauthor Alexander Wiederin <alex@wiederin.xyz> 1790950163 +0200\ncommitter Alexander Wiederin <alex@wiederin.xyz> 1790950163 +0200\n\nkernel: document that btck_WriteBytes may receive a null pointer\n\nThe header does not say whether the bytes pointer can be null when size\nis zero. It can: the writers backed by std::vector pass through\nstd::vector::data(), which may return nullptr for an empty vector, and\nempty elements are ordinary script data.\n\nThis matters for bindings rather than for C callers.\n",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrs4II9Yk79ziwNXEGKsUmoSF5B\nhLD0QSj80cShIsoHYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEZmLhZplht9CJ+3uDlfvI1I9iX3vynDt6Qisdi0P9xFvX/2jSNOH9O4JMjd7Ldlx9\n2uDncmX6hwiwkB21PrNAY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----"
