      "message": "kernel: document that btck_WriteBytes may receive a null pointer\n\nThe header does not say whether the bytes pointer can be null when size\nis zero. It can: the writers backed by std::vector pass through\nstd::vector::data(), which may return nullptr for an empty vector, and\nempty elements are ordinary script data.\n\nThis matters for bindings rather than for C callers.",
